Choose a process boundary and test what its equations can determine (@ic-boundaries: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @industrial-chemistry, #source "../sources/LearnChemE-Process-Self-Study.lingua#r_4KM1THP1QA2SZ5JJ9E1HSMN529", #source "../sources/Chemical-Reactor-Analysis-Rawlings-Ekerdt.lingua#r_7YQAV27Y3J0B537Z6K5HDN8H0A", #source "../sources/Biochemical-Ethanol-Design-Humbird.lingua#r_123G817BYJFAVYGA0ZVK3J5FJH", #industrial-chemistry "../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/practice/Mass-and-component-balances.lingua#r_163GVDJGRJ1DD4JT2398GM371H") { r_2Z2N5W5E8P521QTHQB13KE4R97
**Read:** [LearnChemE — chemical-process self-study modules](../sources/LearnChemE-Process-Self-Study.lingua#r_4KM1THP1QA2SZ5JJ9E1HSMN529), the complete degrees-of-freedom, transient material-balance and reactive material-balance modules; [Chemical Reactor Analysis and Design Fundamentals — Rawlings and Ekerdt](../sources/Chemical-Reactor-Analysis-Rawlings-Ekerdt.lingua#r_7YQAV27Y3J0B537Z6K5HDN8H0A), the full general material-balance derivation and its boundary/steady-state examples; [Biochemical conversion of corn stover to ethanol — Humbird and colleagues](../sources/Biochemical-Ethanol-Design-Humbird.lingua#r_123G817BYJFAVYGA0ZVK3J5FJH), the complete process boundaries and material-account assumptions for one integrated section.

An account states what lies inside, which quantities cross the boundary, which can accumulate and over what interval. A steady state sets the chosen accumulation terms to zero; it does not mean that every local variable is uniform or that a plant's inventory never changes.

For a conserved quantity, accumulation equals input minus output. A species balance additionally includes reaction production/consumption, while an element balance retains conservation when the species change. Define the actual inventory change during startup, shutdown, batch discharge, maintenance or an interrupted campaign before interpreting an apparent recovery.

Count independent unknowns and independent relations, keeping definitions and genuinely additional measurements separate. Duplicating an overall balance already implied by component balances adds no information. A sufficient equation count is necessary for a local solution but does not by itself prove independence, uniqueness, physical feasibility or good conditioning.

**Work:** construct overall, component and unit boundaries for the same published process. Name the unknowns, independent equations and supporting measurements, then show which result remains indeterminate if one observation is removed. Explain how a stock change could mimic changed conversion or recovery, and how an uncertainty-aware measurement would distinguish them.

**Continue:** [Mass and component balances — account for every stream](../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/practice/Mass-and-component-balances.lingua#r_163GVDJGRJ1DD4JT2398GM371H).

**Return:** [Industrial chemistry — chemical transformations, useful products and continuing production](../Industrial-chemistry.lingua#r_3AKBAFB2ABJ0671QW6ZBQ0B618).
